## Findings

- [minor, judge] Invalid LOW_STOCK_THRESHOLD value (spec gap) (criterion C-357020b8): A non-integer value raises ValueError from int() at call time, and the spec doesn't say what should happen. Negative values are also accepted.
- [minor, judge] Tests not isolated from env (criterion C-79953eae): Most tests don't clear LOW_STOCK_THRESHOLD, so an ambient value could make them fail.
- [minor, judge] the judge called a test inadequate (criterion C-79953eae): tests.test_alerts::test_low_stock_message_returns_none_at_threshold

## Feedback

- FB-001: addressed at 0a0be6d7f3: src/inventory/alerts.py:4-6 defines _require_non_negative and low_stock_message calls it.
- FB-002: addressed at 0a0be6d7f3: src/inventory/alerts.py:9-10 reads LOW_STOCK_THRESHOLD as int, default "5"; used at line 15.

